============================================================================================================
POWER -- what these bounds actually support
  TWC        12 independent dates -> honest 95% upper bound  25.00% per date   (the per-triple figure 0.05804% is an artefact of treating one weather day as 430 observations)

  THE TWC STRATUM IS UNDERPOWERED AND MORE HISTORY DOES NOT FIX IT.
  12 independent dates gives a rule-of-three bound of 25% per date. TWC settlement began
  ~2026-08-13, so this stratum grows only with the calendar, at ~21 city-days
  per day. Read a clean TWC result as 'no evidence of a leak', never as
  'the floor holds'. Correction 1 is explicit that the deep archive answers
  seasonality and strategy questions and does not answer this one.

============================================================================================================
WHAT NWS SAYS ABOUT TWC -- the strata are not independent evidence
  The NWS Climatological Report derives from the same ASOS observations IEM
  serves, so its divergence from them was expected to be near-tautological.
  It diverged anyway: 89 of 9,510 NWS city-days have D < 0 (0.936%).

  Applying that rate to the TWC stratum's 247 city-days:
    expected D<0 city-days under the NWS rate : 2.31
    observed  D<0 city-days in TWC            : 0
    P(observing zero | NWS rate)              : 0.098

  So TWC's clean record is entirely consistent with a divergence rate
  this sample cannot detect. If the near-tautological source diverges, the
  prior that a genuinely independent commercial source also goes negative
  given more dates should go UP, not down. Read the TWC stratum as
  'underpowered and so far unfalsified', never as 'the floor holds'.

